      "title": "Rebase vs Merge: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rebase vs Merge: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Merge: Tie the Lines",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Merge makes a ==new commit== with **two parents**",
                "Both histories stay exactly as they happened",
                "{green:Non-destructive}: it only adds history"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rebase: Replay",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Take commits",
                    "sub": "main..feature",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Replay one by one",
                    "sub": "on the new tip",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New SHAs",
                    "sub": "linear history",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Old commits",
                    "sub": "orphaned",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch feature",
                "git rebase main"
              ],
              "note": "replays feature onto main's tip"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rebased commits are ==copies==: same diff and message",
                "{red:Different parent} means a different hash"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Side by Side",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Merge",
                "Rebase"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "History",
                  "adds a merge commit",
                  "==rewritten==, linear"
                ],
                [
                  "Old SHAs",
                  "kept",
                  "orphaned"
                ],
                [
                  "Safety",
                  "non-destructive",
                  "rewrites history"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mental model",
              "text": "Merge = ==tie the two lines together==. Rebase = ==pretend I branched from the latest tip==."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why do rebased commits get new hashes?** The parent changed, so the commit identity changed.",
                "**Which one rewrites history?** Rebase. Merge only adds."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fast-Forward vs Merge Commit",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Fast-Forward vs Merge Commit",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Fast-Forward",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Target has ==no new commits==",
                "Git only ==moves the branch pointer==",
                "{green:No merge commit} is created"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Merge Commit and Flags",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Case",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "No new commits on target",
                  "fast-forward"
                ],
                [
                  "Branches diverged",
                  "merge commit, **two parents**"
                ],
                [
                  "`--no-ff`",
                  "merge commit even if ff possible; branch stays visible"
                ],
                [
                  "`--ff-only`",
                  "refuses unless ff; fails safely on divergence"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Reading the Graph",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Straight line} = fast-forward or rebase",
                "{blue:Diamond} = merge commit"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git log --oneline --graph --all"
              ],
              "note": "diamond shape: a merge commit"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "*   a1f3c9e Merge branch 'feature'",
                "|\\",
                "| * 5d2b7a1 Add login",
                "* | 9c4e8f0 Fix typo",
                "|/",
                "* 3b1a6d2 Init"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Silent default",
              "text": "Plain `git merge` fast-forwards silently. Use `--no-ff` to keep the branch bubble."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why --ff-only?** It fails safely when branches diverged.",
                "**Why --no-ff?** ff is possible, but you want the branch visible.",
                "**Merge commit parents?** Two."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rebase in Practice and Conflicts",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rebase in Practice and Conflicts",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Replay and Conflicts",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rebase ==replays== feature's commits onto the **tip of main**",
                "Replayed commits are new copies with new SHAs"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch feature",
                "git rebase main"
              ],
              "note": "run from feature, not main"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Conflict",
                    "sub": "stops at one commit",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fix files",
                    "sub": "remove markers",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "git add",
                    "sub": "mark resolved",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "--continue",
                    "sub": "next commit",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`git rebase --continue`",
                  "next commit, after `git add`"
                ],
                [
                  "`git rebase --skip`",
                  "{orange:drops} the current commit"
                ],
                [
                  "`git rebase --abort`",
                  "{green:restores} the pre-rebase state"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Undo and Publish",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git reflog` is the ==safety net==: find the pre-rebase SHA",
                "`git reset --hard` to that SHA undoes a bad rebase"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git reflog",
                "git reset --hard <pre-rebase-sha>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "After rebasing a pushed branch",
              "text": "Update it with `git push --force-with-lease`. Never plain `--force`: it can overwrite a teammate's new commits."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Interactive Rebase: Squash, Reword, Drop",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Interactive Rebase: Squash, Reword, Drop",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Todo List",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git rebase -i HEAD~N` opens the last ==N commits==",
                "Listed **oldest first**, edited before replay",
                "Reorder lines = ==reorder commits==",
                "Delete a line = **drop** the commit"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "pick a1b2 add parser",
                "fixup c3d4 typo",
                "reword e5f6 bad subject"
              ],
              "note": "git runs the list top to bottom"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Verbs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Verb",
                "Effect",
                "Message"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`pick`",
                  "keep commit as is",
                  "kept"
                ],
                [
                  "`reword` (`r`)",
                  "keep changes, edit message",
                  "{blue:you edit}"
                ],
                [
                  "`squash` (`s`)",
                  "melt into previous commit",
                  "{green:combined}"
                ],
                [
                  "`fixup` (`f`)",
                  "melt into previous commit",
                  "{red:discarded}"
                ],
                [
                  "`drop` (`d`)",
                  "remove the commit",
                  "gone"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Auto-Arranging Fixups",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`git commit --fixup <sha>` marks a fix for an older commit",
                "`git rebase -i --autosquash` moves it under its target as ==fixup=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git commit --fixup a1b2",
                "git rebase -i --autosquash HEAD~5"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Squash vs fixup",
              "text": "Both fold into the **previous** commit. ==squash== keeps both messages; ==fixup== keeps only the earlier one."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Golden Rule and pull --rebase",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The Golden Rule and pull --rebase",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Golden Rule",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Never} rebase pushed commits of a ==shared branch==",
                "Rebase rewrites hashes, so everyone else must reconcile",
                "==Safe==: your own unpushed or private feature branch",
                "Never rebase `main` or `master`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. pull vs pull --rebase",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "`git pull`",
                "`git pull --rebase`"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Is",
                  "fetch + merge",
                  "fetch + rebase"
                ],
                [
                  "On divergence",
                  "{red:noisy merge commit}",
                  "{green:local commits replayed on origin}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pull.rebase true` makes rebase the ==default== pull",
                "`pull.ff only` makes a pull ==fail== instead of merging"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git config --global pull.rebase true",
                "git config --global pull.ff only"
              ],
              "note": "pick one default"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Shared branch already rebased?",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Fix",
                    "sub": "git pull --rebase",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Check",
                    "sub": "git reflog",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Rebase ==private== history, merge ==shared== history."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "When to Use Which: Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
